From f89d89f4e32db1baf6dcbe82768043a997e9ce6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kai Chen <tingkaic@nvidia.com>
Date: Mon, 11 May 2026 10:33:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] Rate-limit cp2112 GPIO poll error log

cp2112 polls GPIO at 10Hz for interrupt usage. When the underlying USB
HID transfer fails persistently (e.g. device in fail state), the
"error requesting GPIO values: %d" message floods the kernel log at the
same 10Hz cadence, drowning out other journal entries.

Switch the error path in cp2112_gpio_get_all() from hid_err() to
dev_err_ratelimited() so the message is capped at the default kernel
ratelimit (10 messages per 5 seconds) while still surfacing the failure.
The other hid_err() call sites are not on the polled path and are left
unchanged.

Test:
On Strata-BMC, the IO_Board_SMA_[0-3] also flood with the same kernel
error log. The SMA fw version is 0027.01.0201.0000.
